    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d511">

                <pb facs="0609" n="589" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg589"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Pruyn</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 56.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-04"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 4, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your despatch of October 15, (No. 67.) The murder of the French lieutenant,
                    Camus, near <pb facs="0610" n="590" xml:id="pg590"/> Kanagawa, as you have
                    described it, lends a new and shocking aggravation to the relations between
                    Japan and the western powers.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert H. Pruyn</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Kanagawa.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
